# Private product/business strategy — the 20-document foundation pack.
# Deliberately NOT published: it contains overall strategy, monetization and
# niche-selection/competitive scoring. ADRs and AGENTS.md cite these files by
# path; they are available to the team out-of-band, not in this repo.
docs/foundation/

# The audit ledger enumerates defects that are known but not yet fixed. It is
# held out-of-band for the same reason docs/foundation/ is, and because
# publishing a list of open holes helps attackers more than it helps users
# (see SECURITY.md).
docs/audit/

# Vertical documentation is PRIVATE BY DEFAULT and published file by file.
#
# The sensitive material — niche scoring, market sizing, competitive analysis,
# monetization and source-acquisition strategy — is derived from the private
# foundation framework and stays out-of-band. Blanket-ignoring the whole
# directory also buried the docs that SHOULD be public: a vertical's schema, its
# field dictionary, and the methodology behind its sources, freshness and
# quality claims. Those are exactly what a customer needs to evaluate a dataset,
# and withholding them makes the product less trustworthy, not more protected.
#
# So: deny everything, allow by name. A new file is private until someone
# deliberately lists it, which is the right way round for commercial research —
# an allowlist cannot leak a document nobody thought about.
docs/verticals/**
!docs/verticals/**/
!docs/verticals/README.md
!docs/verticals/**/DATA_DICTIONARY.md
!docs/verticals/**/FIELD_DICTIONARY.md
!docs/verticals/**/SCHEMA.md
!docs/verticals/**/SOURCE_METHODOLOGY.md
!docs/verticals/**/FRESHNESS_METHODOLOGY.md
!docs/verticals/**/QUALITY_METHODOLOGY.md
# An explicit public subtree, for anything that does not fit the names above.
!docs/verticals/public/**
